# Monitor profiles: one Lua file per layout you want to switch to, in this folder.

# Give each a unique name ending in .lua, e.g. Mirror.lua, Office.lua, Scale.lua.
# (Suggest not to call one "default" - that name ships with the dotfiles.)

# tip: make the layout with nwg-displays and Apply it, then copy the Lua file it
# writes, ~/.config/hypr/monitors.lua, here under its new name:
#     cp ~/.config/hypr/monitors.lua ~/.config/hypr/Monitor_Profiles/Office.lua
# Only .lua files work: SUPER SHIFT E > Monitor Profiles copies <name>.lua over
# ~/.config/hypr/monitors.lua. (A copy of the hyprlang monitors.conf, which
# nwg-displays still writes too, would be listed but not applied.)

# Picking a profile overwrites ~/.config/hypr/monitors.lua and keeps no backup
# of it - save the current layout as a profile first if you want it back.

# The profile loads on its own, through Hyprland's config auto-reload, unless you
# turned that off. If it does not, log out and back in (seen in virtual machines).
